{"series":{"id":"federal-fiscal-balance::federal-receipts-per-capita-2023","label":"Attributed federal revenue per resident · FFY 2023","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"current U.S. dollars per resident","scope":"us_states","definition":"Published federal receipts per resident; not an individual tax bill.","denominator":"Publisher’s most current Census population estimates for the associated calendar year; updated population vintages in the 2025 report. Published per-capita cells retained; population not inferred from rounded totals.","reporting_period":"Federal fiscal year 2023 (2022-10-01 through 2023-09-30); preliminary publisher estimates","source_url":"https://rockinst.org/issue-area/bop-2025/","sources":[{"id":"rockefeller-federal-balance-2025","title":"Rockefeller Institute of Government · Giving or Getting? 2025","url":"https://rockinst.org/issue-area/bop-2025/","date":"Released August 1, 2025; FFY 2023 preliminary, FFY 2022 revised; historical 2015–2023 vintage","note":"Primary publisher of matched federal fiscal allocation estimates. Federal-budget totals reconciled using state allocators and proxies. Fifty states; DC and territory estimates excluded and unpublished. Not a federal-government official state tax-burden or USAspending-only dataset.","license":"Publicly accessible publisher report; copyright Rockefeller Institute of Government. No explicit open reuse licence identified. Attribute publisher and report; do not treat PDF/design as public domain."}],"limitations":["Detailed matched receipts/spending are FFY 2023 preliminary estimates. FY 2022 and earlier history retain the 2025 report’s revisions; no FY 2024/2025 federal balance is claimed.","The federal fiscal year is October 1 through September 30; per-capita denominators use publisher Census estimates for the associated calendar year.","DC and territories are outside the published tables for 50 states: DC stays explicitly missing in every fiscal map.","These are allocated federal-budget estimates using a mixture of actual data and proxies, sometimes prior-year allocators, not raw tax-collection-location totals.","Included spending covers direct benefits, grants, contracts, wages and COVID relief; national debt interest and other unallocable items are not all assigned to states.","Source printed monetary totals are rounded to millions, per-capita cells to dollars and ratios to 0.01; small arithmetic differences remain rather than rewriting source numbers.","Positive or negative balance is not a state-government budget surplus/deficit, an individual tax bill, an economic impact estimate or a moral ranking. Federal deficit financing means state balances need not sum to zero.","Nominal dollars are not inflation-adjusted. Do not subtract this separate Census state-tax layer from federal spending or compare different fiscal periods as one balance."],"interval_type":null,"display_reference":null,"years":[2023],"places":[{"id":"AL","name":"Alabama"},{"id":"AK","name":"Alaska"},{"id":"AZ","name":"Arizona"},{"id":"AR","name":"Arkansas"},{"id":"CA","name":"California"},{"id":"CO","name":"Colorado"},{"id":"CT","name":"Connecticut"},{"id":"DE","name":"Delaware"},{"id":"DC","name":"District of Columbia"},{"id":"FL","name":"Florida"},{"id":"GA","name":"Georgia"},{"id":"HI","name":"Hawaii"},{"id":"ID","name":"Idaho"},{"id":"IL","name":"Illinois"},{"id":"IN","name":"Indiana"},{"id":"IA","name":"Iowa"},{"id":"KS","name":"Kansas"},{"id":"KY","name":"Kentucky"},{"id":"LA","name":"Louisiana"},{"id":"ME","name":"Maine"},{"id":"MD","name":"Maryland"},{"id":"MA","name":"Massachusetts"},{"id":"MI","name":"Michigan"},{"id":"MN","name":"Minnesota"},{"id":"MS","name":"Mississippi"},{"id":"MO","name":"Missouri"},{"id":"MT","name":"Montana"},{"id":"NE","name":"Nebraska"},{"id":"NV","name":"Nevada"},{"id":"NH","name":"New Hampshire"},{"id":"NJ","name":"New Jersey"},{"id":"NM","name":"New Mexico"},{"id":"NY","name":"New York"},{"id":"NC","name":"North Carolina"},{"id":"ND","name":"No